# Ruling 304: one line ending in the index, always LF.
#
# The mixed regime this replaces was not theoretical. Sessions 14 and 15 each
# lost edits to it: an anchor spanning one LF line and one CRLF line in the same
# file matches under no uniform substitution, which is how it surfaced both
# times. Normalizing kills the class rather than the instances.
#
# Binary pins are the three types actually present, enumerated not guessed:
# 2 png, 4 ttf, 3 woff2. The bat and cmd pins are forward-looking; neither
# extension exists in the tree today, and both genuinely need CRLF if added.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

*.png binary
*.ttf binary
*.woff2 binary
